post.description:
Convert a PlannedWorkorder to a Session with Tasks.

    The session_name becomes the session title, and the planned workorder name
    becomes the session description (subtitle).

    Expected payload:
    {
        "session_name": "Session title (required)",
        "quote_line_ids": ["uuid1", "uuid2", ...],  # Optional: for partial conversion
        "work_blocks": [  # Optional: work schedule blocks
            {
                "start_time": "2024-03-01T09:00:00Z",
                "end_time": "2024-03-01T17:00:00Z",
                "notes": "optional notes"
            }
        ]
    }

Live HTML preview of a quote report — no PDF, no Step Function.

    Two synchronous lambda calls:
      1. dataprep (output_format='html') assembles the full dataset for this
         quote + reporting config and writes it to S3.
      2. workhorse 'render_dataset_html' renders each page to HTML, collapsing
         config loops to first-page + a "(... N more like this)" placeholder.

    Body: { quote_id, reporting_config_id?, type? (default 'quote_standard'), vars? }
    Returns: { success, pages: [ {type:'page', html, label, page_type, render_error?}
                                | {type:'placeholder', page_type, label, more_count} ] }

Live HTML preview of a Plan (Quote v2) report — no PDF, no Step Function.
    Plan twin of quote_preview_html: dataprep (output_format='html') assembles
    the dataset from the plan's LATEST content, then workhorse
    'render_dataset_html' renders each page (loops collapsed).

    Body: { plan_id, reporting_config_id?, type? (default 'plan_standard'), vars? }
    Returns: { success, pages: [...], page_count, job_uuid }

Render a quote document using the quote dataset service.

    Expected payload:
    {
        "quote_id": "uuid",           # Required: Quote to render
        "template_key": "template.docx"  # Required: Template filename in S3
    }

    Returns:
    {
        "success": true,
        "output_url": "https://...",  # Presigned URL to download the rendered document
        "output_key": "adhoc/..."     # S3 key of the output file
    }

get.description:
ZP-2406: per-node power-scheme derivation.

    Returns a label for every node in the SLD indicating the highest-priority
    power source it can reach over the undirected edge graph:
    UPS > Generator > Utility. Unreachable nodes come back as null.

    Response::

        {
          "success": true,
          "data": {
            "sld_id": "...",
            "scheme": {"<node_id>": "UPS"|"Generator"|"Utility"|null, ...}
          }
        }

Options for the work-order asset-scope builder, scoped to this SLD.

    Returns the node classes and rooms that actually appear in the SLD (so the
    dialog only offers usable filters), plus the derivable power schemes::

        {"success": true, "data": {
            "classes": [{"id": "...", "name": "..."}],
            "rooms":   [{"id": "...", "label": "Bldg / Floor / Room"}],
            "power_schemes": ["UPS", "Generator", "Utility"],
            "coms": [1, 2, 3]
        }}

post.description:
Simulate creating an edge and report what the rule engine would
